# sw124, the host who quotes you back (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sw124
revision 1
state ready
dialect saltwell
accent none
tier full
written_for rm_celestine_greatly
written_by claude
title the host who quotes you back
fits stage=adult|old
prefers class=upper temper=even
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk repeats_a_guest_s_own_words_back_word_for_word
likes spiced_cider digging sharp_knife first_snow
dislikes deep_mud haggling
fears a_table_nobody_comes_to
hopes a_house_every_house_still_visits
topics gossip +0.4 friends +0.3 family +0.3 home +0.2 memories +0.2 pastimes +0.2 prices -0.3
styles comfort=formal gossip=exact refuse=cool tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a great house and its long table: gracious, exact and unhurried, with a memory for every word a guest has ever said there and the patience to repeat it at the right moment.

words
oath! = By the long table | On my word and my table | Table and lamp
saying! = A guest leaves something at every table | Words said over bread are words kept | Listen first and you need never ask
table = the long table | my table
guests = my guests | the guests at my table
evenings = my evenings | the evenings at my table
remark = a remark | a thing said in passing
callers = callers | the callers at the door
household = the household | the staff
garden = the garden | the beds behind the house
knife = the paring knife | a knife that keeps its edge
cider = hot cider, spiced | cider with cinnamon in it
firstsnow = the first snow | the year's first snow
mud = mud | the mud of the lower streets
estate = the Estate | these quiet streets
heights = the Heights | the houses up the hill
dryland = the Waste | the dry country I come from
city = the city | this city
lamps = the lamps | the long lamps in the hall
seating = who sits beside whom | the seating
precisely = Precisely | Exactly so
house = the House | our House
growing = where I grew up | where I was raised
chair = a chair | a seat at my table
cook = the cook | my cook
lists = the lists | my morning lists
greathouse = a great house | a house this size
sump = the Sump | the low streets

any
opinion @1 houses for 1 : This city would fall down without the Houses, and that is not a figure of speech. Somebody built #city#. Somebody keeps it standing.
opinion @2 houses for 2 [self.house=greatly_house] : #house.capitalize# laid half the walls of #city#. I don't say it to be thanked. I say it because it's true, and #city# forgets.
opinion @3 dole against 1 [self.wealth=rich|comfortable] : My purse feeds the dole, and the same faces queue twice. #precisely#. I count them, as I count everything.
opinion @4 sump against 2 : Below the rope sheds is not a walk I take by choice. #mud.capitalize# and noise, and nobody who'd be glad to see me.
opinion @5 watch for 1 : #watch.capitalize# keep #estate# quiet of a night. I've never asked more of them than that, and they've never failed it.
opinion @6 times for 1 [self.wealth=rich|comfortable] : Complaining would be foolish, and worse, it would be overheard by #callers#.
opinion @7 merchants mixed 1 : A shop is a #good# thing. A shopkeeper who wants to argue a price at my door is not. Name it once, or leave.
opinion @8 strangers for 1 : #growing.capitalize#, no stranger waited for a name before the bread came. #city.capitalize# could stand to learn that.
opinion @9 city mixed 1 : #city.capitalize# talks before it eats and asks before it listens. I've lived here long enough to forgive it, nearly.
opinion @10 festivals mixed 1 : A feast is #table# for the whole street. I approve of tables. I don't approve of everybody shouting across them.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You're welcome here; sit first, and your name can follow. | #greet#, #address#. Come in from the street.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.house] : #greet#. You find me between #callers#; I can spare you a little time. | #greet#. #household.capitalize# have the hall in hand, so I'm yours a while.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. You're out before the lamps are cold. | #greet#. Not many call on me at this hour.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. #lamps.capitalize# are lit; you're just in time. | #greet#. A late caller. I don't mind it.
line @5 greet [here.outdoors=rain here.region=ridgemere] : #greet#. Leave the wet on the step, if you would. | #greet#. Come in out of that. #mud.capitalize# can stay outside.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Here you are at last. Sit by me, not across. | Good. I've been keeping #chair# for you.
line @1 again.open : Twice today. I'm flattered, and #little# curious. | Back already. #precisely# as I thought you'd be.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : A moment, if you will. I've #remark# to pass on. | Come here. Not too loudly; #guests# are listening.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. I'm glad of you.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Sit; you know where. | #greet#. You've been missed at #table#.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.house] : #greet#. Forgive me if I watch the door. | #greet#. I'm keeping one ear on #household#.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. The evening suits you. | #greet#. Late, and welcome.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Come again; I'll remember where we left it.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Take a lamp from the hall; the street's dark. | #farewell#. Mind #mud# at the foot of the hill.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @2 farewell.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #farewell#. Don't leave it a month. | #farewell#. You'll be at #table# soon, I trust.
line @1 react.news : #surprise#. I hadn't that. Who told you? Never mind; I'll find out. | #surprise#. I'll remember it, and who said it.
line @2 react.news.new : That's news to #table#, and that happens seldom. | #surprise#. Something reached you before it reached #table#.
line @3 react.news.known : I had that before #supper# yesterday. | #knew#. It was said at #table# two nights ago, in nearly those words.
line @4 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. The one who first said it says a good many things. | I'd want it from somebody who saw it, not from #callers#.
line @5 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's grievous. #pity#. | I'm sorry for it. I'll send something to the house. #rest.capitalize#.
line @6 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. I'll see they're asked to #table#. | That's #good# news. It deserves a cup of #cider#.
line @1 answer.how : Well, thank you. #busy.capitalize#, as one is. | #fine#. #household.capitalize# are behaving, and so am I.
line @2 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes self.house] : #busy.capitalize#. Twelve to dine tonight and the fish late. | Run off my feet, politely. #callers.capitalize# since breakfast.
line @1 ask.how : And you? You look as if you've #remark# for me. | How are you keeping, #address#? Honestly, now.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit; you needn't say any more of it. | That's a hard thing. It'll go no further than #table#.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. It's been weathered before, by worse placed than you. | It will look smaller in a week. Most things do, from #chair#.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, but I can't. I've #guests# tonight and the seating isn't settled. | I'd like to, truly. Not this week; #household# needs me at home.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter.capitalize#. I'll ask once more; asking costs me nothing. | Another time. #bc_i_will# I'll keep you to that.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | That's kindly done. #thanks#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect.capitalize#. It was the least a host could do. | Nothing at all. Any host at #table# would have.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #household.capitalize# will be wanting me. | I must see to #seating#. Forgive me.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I've kept you long enough, I think. #excuse#.
line @1 accept_preclose : Of course. Go. | #bc_fair_enough#. Another evening.
line @1 tease.return : You said much the same last spring at #table#. I remember. | Say it at #table# and see who laughs.
line @1 ack : #precisely#. | #bc_it_is#
line @1 give.advice : #advise.capitalize#: say less than you know at a dinner. Someone is always counting. | Never haggle at a door. Name the price once and mean it. #saying#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : I'd not leave the walls this week. #warn#. | Send for an escort, if you must travel beyond #city#. It's cheaper than the other thing.
line @1 confide [self.house] : #vent#: half the Houses come to #table# to find out what the other half know. | #vent#, I keep a book of who sat where, and when. It's never been wrong.
line @1 praise : #wellsaid#. I'll repeat it, with your name on it. | You handled that #precisely# right.
scene word_for_word
when topic=smalltalk|gossip|friends
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : You told me in spring you'd never touch eel. You've had two helpings at #table# tonight. | Last winter you said you'd never go back to that tailor. You're wearing the coat. #precisely#. | You said, at #table#, that you didn't care for cider. You've had two cups.
b : You remember that? | I did say that. | It's a cold night.
a : Every word. It's a habit of #table# I can't break, and don't try to. | You did. #precisely# like that, with a little shrug. | It is. I'll pour you a third #cider#. I'll not remark on it.

scene who_said_what
when topic=gossip|smalltalk self.house self.class=upper
does tell.gossip / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Something was said at #table# last night that I'm still turning over. | #guests.capitalize# think I don't hear what they say behind their cups. I hear the cups too. | #good.capitalize# evening is one where somebody says more than they meant to.
b : What was it? | What do the cups say? | Who was it last night?
a : I shan't repeat it yet. I'll repeat it when it's useful, and to the right ear. | When a cup goes down too fast, the speaker's lying. When it doesn't move, they're frightened. | I'd never say. That's why #guests# come back.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_clever# | #bc_ha#

scene the_seating
when topic=work|friends self.house self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I spent the morning on #seating#. Two of #guests# haven't spoken since a wedding, and one owes the other money. | #seating.capitalize# is harder than running a House. Ask anybody who's done both. | I put the quarrelsome ones side by side. They behave, out of spite.
b : What will you do? | Harder? | Side by side?
a : Put the debtor at my right paw at #table#. Nobody argues money within reach of the host. | Harder. #lists.capitalize# don't take offence at where it's sat. | Side by side, and both of them trying to seem the better guest. It works every time.

scene salon_evening
when topic=pastimes|day self.house here.time=dusk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Lamps are lit and #callers# start within the hour. I like this part best: the quiet before. | Every House in #city# sent word for tonight. Every one. | I've had the cider put on to warm. People talk more freely with something hot in their paws.
b : What's the quiet for? | Even the ones who quarrel? | Do they talk more?
a : Remembering. I go over who said what at #table# last time, so I can ask after it. | Especially those. Nobody wants to be the one talked about in their absence. | Much more. A cold cup makes a careful guest; #cider# makes a talkative one.
b? : #bc_wise# | #bc_ha# | #bc_clever#

scene the_house_walls
when topic=lore|work self.house=greatly_house here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #house.capitalize# laid the walls of #city#, and the bank stands on our ledgers. People forget the first and remember the second. | Brick, tile, lime, stone. Everything in #city# that stands up came through our yards first. | When a wall in #city# cracks, they send to us. When it holds, they forget our name.
b : Which do you mind more? | Everything? | Does that trouble you?
a : The forgetting. Debts are remembered; walls are taken for granted. | Very nearly. Ask any builder whose lime they slake. | It doesn't trouble me. I keep #lists# of both, which is better.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true# | #bc_wise#

scene my_spouse
when topic=family|home self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.spouse# and I have an understanding. I do the talking at #table#, and I'm listened to. | I'd trust #self.spouse# with anything but #seating#. Some gifts are not shared in a marriage. | My #self.spouse_word# says I remember too much. I remember saying that I'd marry anyway.
b : That sounds a happy house. | Which gift? | And you did.
a : Happy enough, and quiet at breakfast, which is rarer in #greathouse#. | Knowing who will quarrel before they've met. #seating.capitalize# can't be taught. | I did. I remind my #self.spouse_word# of it now and then.

scene my_child
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.child# is cleverer than I was at that age, and kinder. I've made my peace with both. | I watch #self.child# at #table# and see my own habits looking back, better mannered. | I worry about #self.child# the way one worries about a lamp left lit: needlessly, and every night.
b : You must be proud. | Better mannered? | Needlessly?
a : Proud, and careful not to say so where #self.child# can hear. | Better. I was sharper. One can be too sharp, like #knife#. | Needlessly. #reassure#, I tell myself. A parent's privilege, not to listen.

scene a_friend_close
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is the one person I don't quote back to. I've never needed to. | If I trust anybody in #city# with my own words, it's #self.friend#. | #self.friend# sits at my left at #table#. The left is for the ones I'd keep.
b : Why not? | That's a short list. | And the right?
a : Because #self.friend# never says a thing that needs repeating. A rare gift at #table#. | Short, and I prefer it, #precisely# so. Long lists of friends are lists of acquaintances. | The right is for the ones I'm watching.

scene the_neighbour
when topic=home|friends self.neighbour
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.neighbour# has the house across from mine. I know the lamp in that window better than my own. | There's no one I'd sooner have across #estate# than #self.neighbour#. | #self.neighbour# is a good neighbour, which means I hear very little through the wall.
b : You watch the window? | High praise. | Little?
a : I notice it. When it's dark early, I wonder. I don't ask #household# either. | It is. I don't give it often. | Very little. A quiet neighbour is worth #cook#.

scene garden_beds
when topic=pastimes|home self.likes=digging here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I dug the bean rows myself this morning. #household.capitalize# were horrified. | There's nothing like an hour in #garden# with my own paws in the earth. Nobody can talk to me there. | #growing.capitalize# nothing grew without a quarrel. Here I put a seed in and the rain does the rest.
b : They'd do it for you. | Nobody? | Easier, then.
a : They would. They'd do it wrong, and I'd not have had the hour. | Nobody dares. It's the only place in #city# I'm not asked a question. | Easier, and less satisfying. I like a thing that has to be argued into growing.

scene paring_knife
when topic=pastimes|home self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep #knife# in my own pocket. #household.capitalize# have theirs, and I have mine. | A dull knife in #greathouse# is a disgrace. I check them myself on Restday. | I hone #knife# every evening. It settles me better than prayer.
b : Why your own? | All of them? | Better than prayer?
a : Because I know where it's been. That's more than I can say for most things on a table. | Every one, and #cook# knows it. Nobody's ever been cut by a sharp knife; it's the dull ones that slip. | The Bright One won't mind. It's a quiet sort of prayer.

scene hot_cider
when topic=food|season self.likes=spiced_cider here.season=autumn|winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I have #cider# brought up when the weather turns. It's the only extravagance I own to. | #cider.capitalize# at dusk, and the day forgives itself. | Cider at #table# loosens tongues better than wine, and nobody wakes ill.
b : Only one? | That's a pretty way to say it. | Better than wine?
a : The only one I'll admit to. The rest at #table# are called hospitality. | Pretty and true. Have a cup, and see. | Better, for my purposes. A guest who wakes ill remembers nothing worth knowing.

scene first_snow
when topic=weather|season here.outdoors=snow here.region=ridgemere self.likes=first_snow
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess / ack
a : Look. #firstsnow.capitalize#. I'll never be used to it. | I'd never seen snow until I came to #city#. I stepped out in my house shoes. | Snow makes #estate# quiet. Even the carriages go softly.
b : It's only snow. | In house shoes? | It's lovely.
a : To you. #growing.capitalize# the sky never gave anything away, least of all this. | And stood in it till my paws ached. I'd do it again. | #bc_it_is# For one morning, every street in #city# looks the same.
b? : #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha# | #bc_true#

scene lower_mud
when topic=weather|travel here.outdoors=rain here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #mud.capitalize# again. One crosses a street and arrives with half of it. | I came back from the market with #mud# to my hocks. #household.capitalize# said nothing, loudly. | #rain.capitalize# I can bear. What it does to #sump# I can't.
b : It's a wet city. | Loudly? | It's worse lower down.
a : #bc_it_is# #growing.capitalize#, a wet street was a feast. I've lost the taste for it. | With their faces. They have very eloquent faces. | Much worse, I'm told. I go round by #estate#.

scene haggling_door
when topic=prices|work self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / insist / ack
a : A carter tried to argue a price at my door with #household# watching this morning. I closed it. | I don't haggle. Name a price; I'll pay it or I won't. Anything else is theatre. | #household.capitalize# know never to bring a bargainer to me. They deal with it at the gate.
b : Did they come back? | Some like the theatre. | Sensible.
a : With a fair price, an hour later. #bc_they_do# | Then they can go to the theatre. My door is not one. | Sensible, and quicker. #saying#.
b? : #bc_good# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_wise#

scene where_i_was_raised
when topic=memories self.away=yes self.from=saltwell
does tell.memory / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In #self.from_town#, nobody talked business until the bread was broken. I keep that still, in #greathouse#. | I grew up in #dryland#, where you remember what's said because nobody writes it down. | Back in #self.from_town# the evenings were the only cool hours. Everyone talked then. I learned to listen there.
b[from=saltwell] #sw : Bread first. My mother did it even for the tax man. | Nobody wrote anything. You kept it in your head or lost it. | The cool hours. You'd sit out till the stars came.
b : Do they notice, here? | Did you learn it there? | Do you miss it?
a@sw : So did mine. He left kinder than he came. #saying#. | Kept it, or lost it. I kept it, #precisely#. | Till the stars, and later. I still keep late hours for it.
a : Some do. Those of #guests# worth knowing ask why. | It's where I learned everything worth keeping. | The quiet. Not the heat. Never the heat.

scene the_accent_dropped
when topic=accent self.away=yes self.from=saltwell self.accent=none
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I left my home vowels at the gate of #city# the year I came. I've not been sure since whether that was wise. | People in #heights# can't place me. I prefer it. A voice that can't be placed can't be dismissed. | I still wait a breath before I answer. It's the only thing of home in my speech now.
b : You'd not know it. | Can't be dismissed? | I'd noticed that.
a : No. That was rather the point, #precisely#. | They try. They can't place me, so they listen. | You'd be one of very few. I'm obliged to you for saying.

scene stars_over_the_roofs
when topic=weather|day here.time=night here.outdoors=clear here.region=ridgemere
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : A clear night. Rare in #city#. At home there were more stars than sky. | I'll stand at the window a while. #household.capitalize# think I'm checking the street. | When it's clear I can see #lamps# of #city# right down to the water. They're the city's stars.
b : More stars than sky? | Aren't you? | That's well put.
a : #precisely#. You'd not believe it unless you'd stood under it. | Partly. One can look up and keep an eye down. | It's the one kindness #city# does me on purpose.

scene grey_morning
when topic=weather|day here.outdoors=fog here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fog. #heights# disappear and the whole city pretends to be equal. | In fog I can't see who's coming to the door till they knock. I find I mind it. | A grey morning. #guests# will arrive damp and cross, and stay late to dry.
b : For a morning. | You like to know first? | Late's good for you.
a : For a morning. It's refreshing, briefly. | #bc_always# A host who's surprised is a host who's not prepared. | Late is when things get said. I'll have #cider# put on.

scene heights_society
when topic=gossip|friends self.class=upper here.region=ridgemere
does tell.gossip / react.self / insist
a : There are perhaps forty wolves in #heights# worth knowing, and they all know each other's business. I know it a little better. | Society here is #table#, and everyone's watching the salt. | I've heard a thing about a House that would empty half the chairs in #city#. I'll keep it.
b : Better how? | The salt? | Will you tell anyone?
a : They tell me. Then they tell each other what they told me, slightly wrong. I keep the right version. | Who passes it to whom, and who's left reaching. It says everything. | Not yet. A thing like that is worth more kept than spent.

scene topic_gossip
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.news / assess / ack
a : I'm told #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'd heard a version of it before supper; this is the better version. | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Whoever said it first meant something by it. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#, or so it goes round. #precisely# the sort of thing that's never quite as said.
b : Is it true? | Does it matter who? | You think it's wrong?
a : True enough to repeat carefully at #table#. Not true enough to repeat loudly. | #bc_always# The first teller is the one who meant something by it. | Wrong in the details. They always are, by the third telling.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true#

scene gossip_grief
when topic=gossip|news topic.claim_kind=death
does tell.news / sympathise / assess
tone grave / tender / even
a : I heard that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll send to the house this evening. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. I'm sorry to have it from the street and not from the family. | Word is that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. There'll be an empty chair somewhere tonight.
b : #sympathy#. | It's sad news. | That's hard.
a : Something plain. Bread and a lamp, the way it was done #growing#. | Sad, and it'll be talked about badly. I'll say nothing more of it. | Hard. Empty chairs are the hardest thing #table# holds.

scene gossip_wedding
when topic=gossip|news topic.claim_kind=marriage
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll need to think again about #seating#. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#. Good. I'd seen it coming across #table# since spring. | I hear #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's one quarrel ended, and two families obliged to dine together.
b : You'll ask them both? | Since spring? | Is that good?
a : Both, side by side, and nobody else between them for once. | They passed the salt a little too carefully. One notices. | #bc_very_good# Obliged families make the best #guests#.

scene hard_times_below
when topic=times|prices world.times=hard|lean self.wealth=rich|comfortable
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : Fewer lamps in the windows below the hill this month. One notices from up here. | #household.capitalize# say the bread's gone up again. I've told them to send what's left over down the hill. | Hard times are when people stop coming to #table#. I've had three regrets this week.
b : That's kind. | Kind of you. | Three?
a : It's observant. Kindness would be doing something about it. | Not kind. Bread that isn't eaten is a sin, my #gran# said. | Three. I'll call on them instead, with #cider#. A guest who can't come is a guest who's worried.

scene good_times_above
when topic=times world.times=good|boom
does tell.news / react.news / assess
a : Coin's moving. Every House wants a dinner, and every dinner wants a better one than the last. | Good times. #callers.capitalize# arrive in new coats and pretend they're old ones. | When the times are good the talk at #table# gets louder and says less.
b : Good for you, surely. | Pretend? | Less?
a : #good.capitalize# for #cook#. I'd rather have the quieter years; people say more in them. | They brush them to look worn. I notice the price tags they forgot. | Less worth remembering. #bc_i_know# I remember it anyway.

scene below_the_hill
when topic=smalltalk|travel here.region=ridgemere
does give.opinion / ask.opinion / insist / ack
a : The rope sheds are as low as I walk. Not pride; #mud#. | People think #estate# is cut off from the rest. We're not. Everything below comes up the hill as news. | I sent a basket down to #sump# once. It came back empty, with a note. I kept the note.
b : Is it only the mud? | As news? | What did it say?
a : Mostly. And being stared at. One gets enough of that at one's own table. | By supper. The lower streets talk faster than the upper ones, and better. | That the basket was welcome and the next should have salt in it. I thought that was #precisely# right.
b? : #bc_true# | #bc_ha# | #bc_good#

scene faith_quiet
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I go to chapel on Restday and listen, mostly for which #guests# aren't there. | Every morning I give the Bright One thanks for water. Nobody raised where I was raised ever stops. | The Bright One sees every table. I try to set mine as if that were so.
b : That's one way to pray. | Every morning? | That's a high bar.
a : It's mine. The Bright One knows where to find me: at #table#. | Every morning, even in a city that never runs dry. Especially here. | #bc_it_is# I don't always clear it. I try.

scene dreams_at_table
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I dreamt last night #table# was laid and nobody came. I woke and counted the invitations. | I dream of sand sometimes. Miles of it, and one cup of water, and nobody to give it to. | I dreamt all #guests# I've ever had said the same sentence at once. I couldn't remember it.
b : Had they all answered? | Nobody at all? | What was the sentence?
a : All but two. I'll be sending #callers# again. | Nobody. I'd give it to the first who came. I always would. | That's what woke me. Not remembering. It's never happened awake.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_ha#

scene a_host_s_health
when topic=health self.age>=45
does tell.self / react.self / reassure
a : My knees mind the stairs more than they did. There are a great many stairs in #greathouse#. | I've a cough from the damp in #garden#. I'll not stop digging for it. | I sleep less than I did. I lie awake going over who said what at #table#. A poor habit.
b : Take the stairs slowly. | Rest it, then. | A poor habit?
a : I take them slowly and #household# call it dignity. | I'll rest it in the evening, with #cider#. | A poor habit, and the reason I'm never surprised. I'll keep it.

scene newcomer_place
when topic=newcomer here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : There's a new face in #estate#. I've already asked three people who it belongs to. | Somebody new took the house at the end of #estate#. No callers yet. I'll be the first. | A newcomer asked me the way this morning and told me half their life before I'd pointed.
b : Did they know? | Why first? | Which half?
a : Two of #callers# guessed. One knew, and didn't know they knew. That's usually the way. | Because the first caller sets the tone. And because I want to see inside. | The half they'll regret telling, I imagine. I'll be kind with it.
b : #bc_ha# | #bc_wise# | #bc_good#

scene festival_table
when topic=festival|season
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : On a feast day I open the kitchen door to the lane. A table should be long enough for the whole street, once a year. | A festival is #table# nobody seated. That's why it ends in quarrels. | I'll put up lamps for the feast and keep my own counsel indoors. Everybody else will say plenty.
b : The whole street? | Ends in quarrels? | Plenty?
a : The whole street. Where I come from, nobody ate a feast alone. | #bc_always# Seat people badly and they'll find something to dispute. | Plenty, and most of it to somebody who'll repeat it to me by Restday.

scene invitations
when topic=work|pastimes self.house self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I've written twenty invitations for #table# this morning, every one by my own paw. | An invitation is a sentence. It has to say yes, and also who else is coming, without saying either. | I never invite on the same day I hear a quarrel. One waits a week, and sees who's still angry.
b : By paw? All twenty? | Without saying it? | A week?
a : All twenty. A clerk's hand, to #guests#, says the invitation is a duty. Mine says it's a wish. | In the paper, the hour, the seal. People read all three. | A week. By then the angry one at #table# has usually done something to regret.

story the_first_dinner [topic=memories|friends self.away=yes self.from=saltwell self.age>=30]
  : My first dinner in #city#, the guests began talking before they'd eaten a thing. I sat there waiting for somebody to break the bread.
  : Nobody did. So I stood, broke it myself, and passed it down the whole table. The host looked as though I'd struck him.
  : Afterwards three #guests# asked to call on me. I'd not said a word all night.
  ask : Would you have broken it, in my place?
  b : I'd have sat and waited, and been thirsty.
  b[from=saltwell] : Of course. Nobody eats before the bread's shared.

story the_misquoted_merchant [topic=gossip|pastimes self.house]
  : A merchant from the coast told my table one spring that he'd never sell a ship to a House. Every word, I remember.
  : The next winter he sat in the same chair and boasted of the ship he'd sold to one.
  : I said: you told us last spring you never would. I gave him the day, and the dish, and the wine.
  : He didn't come back. I didn't ask him to.
  b : You remembered the dish? | That's sharp of you.
  b[class=upper] : I've seen you do that. I've learned to choose my words at your table.

story the_listening_lesson [topic=memories|lore self.from=saltwell self.age>=25]
  : My #gran# used to sit by the town well and listen to everything said over the buckets.
  : She told me a promise is only as good as the one who heard it. So be the one who heard it.
  : I've been that one at #table# ever since. It's served me better than any dowry.
  ask : Has anybody ever kept your words for you like that?
  b[old] : One or two. They're gone now, and my words with them.
  b : Not that I know of. That's a thought, though.

story the_snow_year [topic=weather|memories here.region=ridgemere self.likes=first_snow]
  : The first winter I spent here, I woke to everything white and thought the house had burned to ash in the night.
  : I ran out into the street in my nightclothes. A carter laughed at me and threw a snowball.
  : I've had #snow# every winter since. I still go out to it first thing, properly dressed now.
  b : A snowball? At you? | You thought it was ash?
  b[from=saltwell] : I did the same. Everyone from home does.

story the_knife_from_home [topic=pastimes|memories self.likes=sharp_knife self.away=yes]
  : My #dad# gave me a little knife the day I left home. Said a sharp blade and a long memory would see me anywhere.
  : I've had it honed every week since. It's cut more bread in #city# than it ever did at home.
  : Every great house I've been in has better silver. Not one has a better knife.
  ask : Have you something you'd never part with, from a parting?
  b : A coat, worn to threads. I'll not part with it.
  b[from=ridgemere] : I've never left home. Perhaps that's why I keep nothing.

rule @hall_orders
when concept=bark working=yes self.house
does aside
cooldown 6h
say The blue room for the late #guests#, not the green. | More lamps in the hall. #guests.capitalize# can't talk in the dark.

rule @lamplight
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #lamps.capitalize#. Now the evening begins. | Dusk. Put #cider# on.

rule @snow_bark
when concept=bark here.outdoors=snow here.region=ridgemere self.likes=first_snow
does aside
cooldown 12h
say There it is. #firstsnow.capitalize#. | Snow on the steps. Leave it till noon; I want to look at it.

rule @mud_bark
when concept=bark here.outdoors=rain here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=deep_mud
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #mud.capitalize# on the hall floor again. Boots off at the door, please. | Half of #sump# has come in on someone's hem.

rule @bargain_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.dislikes=haggling
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Name it once, and we'll see. #saying#. | Nobody argues a price on this step. #oath#.

rule @memory_bark
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Last spring, at #table#. Yes. I remember. | That's not what was said at #table#. Not quite.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Sit first; then tell me what brings you. | #greet#, #address#. Mostly I'll listen; begin when you like.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. I remember our last talk, every word. What is it today? | #topic.player#. Welcome back. Take #chair#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : #greet#. It's late, but the lamps are still lit. Say what's needed.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : #greet#. You're in a house that remembers. Be brief, and be civil.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.house] : I keep #self.workplace#: the rooms, #household#, #table#, and #seating#, the hardest of them. | #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I keep a house, and I keep its memory.
dlg @2 resident.job : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. It asks more care than it looks, #precisely# as much as a table. | I keep things in order and listen while I do it. #saying#.
dlg @1 resident.business [business=thriving] : Thriving. Every chair at #table# filled, and more asking. I'll not complain.
dlg @2 resident.business [business!=thriving|failing] : Steady, thank you. #household.capitalize# are paid and the lamps are lit.
dlg @3 resident.business [business=failing] : Not well. A stranger gets no more than that from #table#.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. It was said at #table# last night, more or less.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : All #estate# is talking of #world.event_words#. I've heard four versions; I believe the second.
dlg @3 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Nothing that would bear repeating to a guest. | Nothing yet. Ask me after #supper#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | I hear a great deal at #table# and repeat very little. That's why I go on hearing it.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : It's said that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'll not swear to the details, #precisely#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I'll remember what you said. | #farewell#, #address#. Come again; there's always a chair.
dlg @1 master.learn [here.teaches=yes self.house] : You'd learn to keep #greathouse#? It's #lists#, patience and a long memory. Ask. | Keeping a great house can be taught. Remembering can only be practised. Ask.
dlg @2 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : #here.trade_title.capitalize#? I can show you. Watch first, and ask after.
dlg @1 master.work [self.house] : Long days. Lists in the morning, #callers# all afternoon, #table# at night. You'll remember everything, or you'll be no use to me. | It's never finished. #callers.capitalize# are always arriving.
dlg @2 master.work : Steady #work#, and more care in it than you'd think. Watch, and you'll see.
dlg @1 master.wages : A learner draws no #money# here. You work beside me and learn it in a third of the time; what it earns you after is yours.
dlg @1 master.takes [here.take_on=yes] : I take a single learner, someone I know and trust. You'd do. Ask, and #household# will make room.
dlg @2 master.takes [here.take_on=no] : I take a single learner, someone I know and trust. #here.take_on_why#
dlg @1 master.taken : Good. Come at first light and bring nothing but a clean coat and a quiet tongue. | Settled. We begin with #lists#. Everything begins there.
dlg @1 master.refused : #topic.why# | Not yet. #topic.why#
dlg @1 master.bye : #farewell#. Remember what you saw today. | #farewell#. Come back when you've practised.
graft resident.hub
choice Is it true you remember everything said at your table? -> remember
node remember
say Everything worth remembering, and most of what isn't. Where I grew up nothing was written; you kept it in your head or lost it. I kept it.
mood calm
free
choice What did I say, last time? -> remember_me
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node remember_me
say Every word. I'll not repeat it here. One day it'll matter, and then I'll repeat it exactly, and you'll be glad I kept it.
choice I'll choose my words, then. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft resident.job
choice How do you decide who sits where? [self.class=upper] -> seats
node seats
say Debtors beside the host. Quarrels side by side, so each must seem the better guest. Old friends apart, so they talk to somebody new. The rest by rank.
mood formal
choice And where would you put me? -> seats_me
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node seats_me
say Near the end, in plain view of me. Not as a slight. The end of a table hears everything said along it.
choice I'll take that. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
